Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:01:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 378/488] DeepSeek-V4.1: the TileLang embedding takes a row a
 block on long prefill chunks

Below 512 tokens a row stays spread over five blocks, a piece a thread, so a
decode step's few tokens put every load in flight at once; from 512 tokens a row
is one block, each thread's five pieces loaded before any is stored: the 8K
prefill chunk was 40,960 blocks of one load each and +0.7% against vLLM's CUDA
kernel. Both layouts are declared; the bytes are unchanged.
